COMMAND NAME: mppcreatecluster.sh

Initializes a Bizgres MPP array by using configuration
parameters specified in a mpp_config_file.

*****************************************************
SYNOPSIS
*****************************************************

mppcreatecluster -c <mpp_config_file> [-h <host_file>] [-p 
<postgresql_conf_mpp_additions>] [-s <standby_master_host>] [-o] 
[-a] [-q] [-l <logfile_directory>]

mppcreatecluster [-? | -v]


*****************************************************
DESCRIPTION
*****************************************************

The mppcreatecluster script will create a Bizgres MPP DBMS 
instance using the values defined in a Bizgres MPP configuration 
file (see mpp_config_example).

The functionality of mppcreatecluster is analogous to 
PostgreSQLs initdb script, which creates the data storage 
directories, generates the shared catalog tables and configuration files, 
and creates a template database, which is a template used to create 
other databases. 

In a Bizgres MPP DBMS, each database instance (the master and all 
segments) must be initialized across all of the hosts in the system
in such a way that they can all work together as a unified DBMS.
The mppcreatecluster script takes care of initializing 
the database on the MPP master and on each segment instance, and 
configuring the system as a whole.


*****************************************************
OPTIONS
*****************************************************

-c <mpp_config_file>

Required. The full path and filename of the MPP configuration 
file, which contains all of the defined parameters to configure 
the array. See mpp_config_example for a description of this file.

-h <host_file>

Optional. The full path and filename of a file that contains 
the host names of all the hosts in the array (master host and all 
segment hosts). If not specified on the command line, you can specify
the host file using the MACHINE_LIST_FILE parameter in the 
mpp_config_file.

-p <postgresql_conf_mpp_additions>

Optional. The name of a file that contains global postgresql.conf 
parameter settings needed for Bizgres MPP. These settings will be 
used when the individual master and segment instances are started. 
If not specified, then the default values defined in 
./postgresql_conf_mpp_additions will be used.

-s <standby_master_host>

Optional. If you wish to configure a backup master host, specify 
the host name using this option.

-o

Creates a master instance only. Does not configure any segment hosts.

-a

Do not prompt the user for confirmation.

-q

Run in quiet mode. Command output is not displayed on the screen, 
but is still written to the log file.

-l <logfile_directory>

The directory to write the log file. Defaults to 
<current_directory>/logs.

-?

Displays the online help.

-v

Displays the version, status, last updated date, and checksum 
of this script.

*****************************************************
EXAMPLES
*****************************************************

Initialize a Bizgres MPP array:

./mppcreatecluster.sh -c mpp_config

Display the online help for the mppcreatecluster script:

./mppcreatecluster.sh -?


